schema: "0.4"
id: chalkboard-01-query-and-answer
type: image
quality: high

# The Robot Learns — a terminal study CLI that answers questions calibrated to your
# expertise. Query & Answer screen (the /query slash-command output) — the flagship surface.
# Theme tenets: always-dark forest-green slate board, warm chalk-white hand-lettering, dusty
# colored-chalk accents used categorically (never neon), flat radius-0 board, dashed chalk
# rules + hand-drawn underlines/arrows for emphasis (never bold weight).
# Palette: board green #2d4a2d, near-black board #1e2a1e, chalk-white #e8e4d8, sand-chalk
# #c8c0a8, yellow chalk #e8d44c, blue chalk #6cb4dc, rose chalk #e06060, sage chalk #50b878.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity UI mockup of a warm,
    always-dark TERMINAL session skinned as a professor's chalkboard — a single focused
    terminal window, not a web page and not a browser. The register is the front row of a
    great lecture: a dark forest-green slate board the tutor writes on, warm chalk-white
    lettering, a few sticks of colored chalk for emphasis. The agent's explanatory answer is
    hand-lettered in a casual print-handwriting face, as if drawn out on the board; the typed
    command line, code and technical values stay in a neat monospace like chalked equations.
    Emphasis is an underline or a drawn arrow, never a bold weight. Colored chalk is dusty and
    desaturated, never neon. Flat board, square corners, dashed chalk rules between regions,
    a faint dust of chalk texture.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity mockup of a focused single-pane TERMINAL session — "The Robot
    Learns", a study CLI — skinned as a dark green chalkboard, showing the output of a /query
    command. One warm forest-green slate board fills the whole frame like a terminal window.
    NO browser chrome, NO tabs, NO address bar, NO web page.

    OVERALL LAYOUT: one immersive board top-to-bottom with a slim right context margin.

    TOP is a monospace COMMAND LINE — a yellow-chalk prompt caret and the typed question,
    "> robot-learns  why does a transformer need positional encoding?".

    The dominant CENTER is the CALIBRATED ANSWER BLOCK — the tutor's answer hand-lettered in
    warm chalk-white, two short roomy paragraphs. One key term carries a wavy hand-drawn
    yellow-chalk underline, and a hand-drawn chalk arrow curves from a small margin note to
    that line. One compact fenced code-and-equation snippet sits in monospace on a slightly
    lighter green board panel outlined with a dashed chalk rule.

    A slim RIGHT MARGIN about a quarter of the width carries ambient context: an EXPERTISE
    LEVEL BADGE drawn as a small chalk-outlined tag reading "Transformers · Intermediate", and
    below a dashed chalk rule a MACHINE / ENVIRONMENT PROFILE card listing OS, shell and
    toolchain in muted chalk monospace.

    BELOW THE ANSWER, RELATED TOPICS appear as a row of small chalk-outlined chips reading
    "attention", "embeddings", "rotary encoding". A VERBOSITY / DEPTH control sits as a
    three-segment chalk scale "beginner · normal · deep" with the middle segment underlined in
    bright chalk to show it is active. A faint monospace status line reads
    "saved to board · article kb-1042 · follow-ups keep context".

    PALETTE & TYPE: a deep forest-green slate board as the canvas, one slightly lighter green
    panel where the code strip and margin lift; lettering in warm dusty chalk-white, secondary
    labels in dimmer sand-chalk, faint labels in muted olive-chalk. Emphasis and categories in
    sticks of dusty colored chalk — a soft rose-red, a dusty sky-blue, a warm butter-yellow, a
    sage green — all desaturated like real chalk, never bright or neon, each used the way a
    teacher reaches for a different stick. The answer prose is hand-lettered in a casual print
    handwriting face; the command, code, ids and technical values in a neat monospace.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: flat board with square corners, no rounded cards and no glossy panels;
    regions divided by dashed chalk rules rather than solid boxes; a boxed concept is a
    hand-drawn chalk outline with slightly uneven edges, not a filled card; a faint even dust
    of chalk grain across the board and one soft eraser smudge.

    MOOD: warm, academic, personal — the aha moment drawn out in colored chalk, think-aloud
    teaching, unhurried and roomy, the best class you ever took.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI, browser chrome, address bar, browser tabs, web page, rounded cards, glossy panels, neon or saturated colors, dry-erase whiteboard, pure white or light background, bold heavy type"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Matches the Query & Answer screen: mono command line, hand-lettered calibrated answer with a code snippet, expertise-level badge, machine/environment profile, related-topics chips, verbosity control — all inside one terminal board"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Always-dark forest-green board, warm chalk-white handwriting prose + mono code, dusty categorical colored-chalk accents (no neon), flat square corners, dashed chalk rules and hand-drawn underline/arrow — not generic UI defaults"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Clear reading hierarchy, dominant answer column with a slim context margin, plausible real-product terminal layout"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"
    - "browser chrome, tabs, or address bar instead of a terminal window"
    - "neon or saturated colors, or a light/whiteboard background"

tags: [chalkboard, therobotlearns.com, screen-mockup, terminal]
